WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.433
Welcome back, creators!

00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:11.300
This is the lesson where everything comes together.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:18.033
Here are our three files. index.html gives the structure.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:21.367
style.css makes it beautiful.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:25.433
And script.js brings it to life.

00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:27.633
They each have their own job,

00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:30.867
but they work together as one team.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:35.300
Every game starts with a fresh deck.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:39.967
createDeck receives a pairCount, like 6.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:44.233
Array.from makes the numbers 1 to 6.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.100
Then, the three dots, called the spread operator,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.367
copy those numbers twice into one array.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:54.933
Six pairs, twelve cards.

00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:58.833
Next, shuffle mixes them up.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.867
It starts at the last card,

00:01:00.867 --> 00:01:04.867
picks a random position, and swaps the two cards.

00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:07.200
Then it moves one step to the left,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.900
and does it again, all the way to the start.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.967
Math.random picks a random number,

00:01:13.967 --> 00:01:16.667
so every game is different!

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:23.467
Now, let's turn over some cards. Here's flipCard.

00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:28.167
When a card is clicked, flipCard receives that exact card.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:32.233
That's how the game knows which one was chosen.

00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:35.467
First, a safety check.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.600
If the board is locked, or the card is already face up

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.767
or matched, we stop right there, with return.

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:46.900
Otherwise, we add the class is-flipped.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:50.567
And our CSS spins the card around!

00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:53.100
If there is no first card yet,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.067
this card becomes the first card, and we wait for another click.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:00.667
If there already is a first card,

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:03.433
this one becomes the second card.

00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:07.800
We add one to moves, and check for a match.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:11.133
And while two cards that don't match are

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:13.467
being shown, lockBoard is true.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:18.167
So a third card can't be turned over until they flip back.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:23.267
Here is the heart of our game: checkForMatch.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:27.567
It compares the numbers stored on the two cards.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.833
If they match, both cards get the

00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:33.533
class is-matched, and turn green.

00:02:33.533 --> 00:02:38.133
They stay face up, and matchedPairs goes up by one.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.533
If they don't match,

00:02:40.533 --> 00:02:44.633
we lock the board, and wait 850 milliseconds.

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:47.167
That's less than one second.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:50.667
Then we turn both cards back over.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:55.033
Finally, resetTurn clears the first and second card,

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:59.033
and unlocks the board, ready for the next turn.

00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:01.967
Watch the moves counter.

00:03:01.967 --> 00:03:06.967
Every time we turn over two cards, it goes up by one.

00:03:07.933 --> 00:03:10.733
Now, the timer.

00:03:10.933 --> 00:03:15.000
The timer starts the very first time a card is flipped.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.333
setInterval runs a little piece of code every

00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:21.633
1000 milliseconds, which is one second.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.800
Each time, seconds goes up by one,

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.067
and formatTime shows it as minutes and seconds.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:32.733
And here's the progress bar.

00:03:32.733 --> 00:03:35.900
updateStats sets its width to

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.900
matchedPairs ÷ totalPairs × 100%.

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:45.467
Three pairs out of six? The bar is half full!

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:48.267
Great games give feedback,

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:51.333
so players know what's happening.

00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:55.067
Our sounds don't come from audio files.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:04:00.433
The browser makes them itself, using the Web Audio API.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.233
playTone creates a tiny musical note.

00:04:04.233 --> 00:04:07.800
A short, bright note for a flip...

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.100
...a higher, happy note for a match...

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:17.100
...and a low, gentle note when the cards don't match.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:22.633
The message under the grid gives feedback with words, too.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:26.867
Players can choose their challenge.

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:32.067
Easy has four pairs. Medium has six.

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.833
And Challenge has eight.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.767
When the player picks a new level,

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:40.800
the change event runs startNewGame.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.867
startNewGame resets everything:

00:04:43.867 --> 00:04:47.700
the moves, the timer, and the matched pairs.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.600
Then it builds a fresh board.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.067
The Restart button and the Play again

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:55.900
button run the very same function.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.867
That's the beauty of functions:

00:04:57.867 --> 00:05:01.200
write once, use everywhere.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:05.300
Now, the final pair.

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:11.533
When matchedPairs equals totalPairs, finishGame runs.

00:05:11.733 --> 00:05:14.500
It stops the timer, shows the final moves

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.400
and time, plays a little three note tune,

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.733
and shows the celebration screen!

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.600
And there it is!

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.767
Your cards can flip, your game can recognise matching numbers,

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:33.167
your timer can count, and your progress can change.

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:37.133
We have turned our code into a real game!

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.433
But before we call ourselves game

00:05:39.433 --> 00:05:43.167
creators, we have one final mission.

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:48.433
Let's test, improve, and personalise our creation!
